                            <comment id="205672" author="jamesanunez" created="Thu, 17 Aug 2017 20:51:02 +0000">&lt;p&gt;It looks like the patch for &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-7497" title="conf-sanity test_32b: FAIL: list verification failed and test_32b failed with 4 " class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-7497"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-7497&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/#/c/25940/" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/#/c/25940/&lt;/a&gt;. fixed this issue by not turning on the MGS service in the disk image. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I'm not closing this ticket because it looks like more work is necessary. From the commit message of 25940:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;It turned out that the MGS svc was wrongly turned on in disk image
'disk2_4-zfs.tar.bz2', which caused the OST mount failure with
EALREADY because the MGS service has already been started by the MDS.

This is just a temporary solution and the final fix would be to clean
the disk image in question.
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="498324" author="adilger" created="Wed, 22 Jul 2026 09:09:48 +0000">&lt;p&gt;The disk2_4 image was removed in 2.16 in patch  &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/47281" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/47281&lt;/a&gt; ("&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-10215" title="disk2_5-ldiskfs.tar.bz2 is not packaged into test rpm" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-10215"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-10215&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; tests: remove disk2_4 disk2_5 images")&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                    </comments>
